// Title: HackTool - PurpleSharp Execution
// Sigma ID: ff23ffbc-3378-435e-992f-0624dcf93ab4
// Status: test | Level: critical
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-06-18 | Modified: 2023-02-05
// ATT&CK: T1587, resource-development
// Description: Detects the execution of the PurpleSharp adversary simulation tool
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/mvelazc0/PurpleSharp
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_purplesharp_indicators.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "\\purplesharp" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "PurpleSharp.exe") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "xyz123456.exe" or ProcessCommandLine contains "PurpleSharp")
